cbm 0.4.1 (unreleased)
	   * Added macOS support: interface statistics come from the sysctl(3)
	     NET_RT_IFLIST2 interface on macOS (/proc/net/dev on Linux), and the
	     interface address lookup now uses getifaddrs(3) instead of the
	     SIOCGIFADDR ioctl on all platforms. CI also builds and runs the tests
	     on macOS 14 and 15.
   * Fixed interfaces being culled from the display on every update
     (regression in the uninitialized-statistics fix) and during the
     warmup window; interfaces now persist from the first frame.
   * Fixed counter resets and non-positive time deltas producing huge
     speed spikes and permanently polluted peak statistics.
   * Gave each interface its own warmup counter, so late-appearing
     interfaces get correct peak warmup.
   * Extracted /proc/net/dev parsing into a testable function and added
     a unit test suite (automake TESTS, 27 checks).
   * Fixed unchecked strcpy into ifr_name and unhandled inet_ntop
     failure in the interface address lookup.
   * Fixed the VerticalTable include guard and the Interface detail
     value cell style.
   * Added a .gitignore and dropped the destructive distclean-local
     rules; pristine sources are restored with ./autogen.sh clean.
   * Check for the ncurses library at configure time and build with
     -Wall -Wextra (fixing all surfaced warnings, including %Lu
     sscanf conversions).
   * Documented the Linux-only platform requirement and the interactive
     keys (including the p/n aliases) in README and the manpage; added
     a manpage key check to the release checklist.
   * Distribute cbm.txt, create-man.sh and cbm.1 in dist tarballs.
   * Updated CI: actions/checkout@v4, Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 matrix,
     gcc/clang builds with make check, and an ASan+UBSan job.

cbm 0.4 - 26 Mar. 2025
   * Increased max rows to display from 8 to 64. Thanks to Jason Bowen
     <jbowen@infinitecactus.com>.
   * Implemented peak bandwidth statistics. Thanks to David Polverari
     <david.polverari@gmail.com>.
   * Removed EXTRA_DIST from Makefile.am.

cbm 0.3.2 - 15 Aug. 2021
